    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math>&nbsp;be functions defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is the maximum of the powers of those primes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>. Then, the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
